cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the base-9 result, please cite it as below."
title: "Self-similar reverse-and-add cycles and a base-9 Lychrel family"
authors:
  - family-names: "Kusayama"
    given-names: "Yuki"
version: "2026.11.27"
date-released: 2026-11-27
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23289048
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/dew-web/lychrel-self-similar"
keywords:
  - reverse-and-add
  - Lychrel numbers
  - 196 problem
  - palindromes
  - finite automata
abstract: >-
  Programs, proofs and data on the reverse-and-add (196) problem.
  The first version (11 October 2026, doi:10.5281/zenodo.23289049) gives an explicit
  infinite family N(m) of base-9 Lychrel numbers with a center string, proved for all m >= 2,
  and an exact finite-automaton search for two-run self-similar cycles.
  This version adds results first published on GitHub on 21 November 2026:
  two-run Lychrel families in bases 50, 77, 98, 146, 235, 306, 390 and 467, each proved for
  all run lengths (bases 50, 98 and 146 were proved earlier by mizopl,
  doi:10.5281/zenodo.23468033); the nonexistence of two-run cycles in base 10 for periods
  2-23; statistics of the palindrome decay rate by overflow history; and a two-ended window
  model that reproduces the digit growth rate of 196 (0.41394 per step).
  Discovery dates and related work: docs/PRIORITY.md.
